<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibrahim Tamghach Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1068">1068</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ibrahim ibn Nasr</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibrahim Tamghach Khan, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasr-ibn-ali">Nasr ibn Ali</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kara-khanid-khanate">Kara-Khanid Khanate</a> divided around 1042 and founded the Western Kara-Khanid Khanate with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarkand">Samarkand</a>. He built a strong, centralised state, founded a hospital and a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasa</a> in Samarkand, and was remembered as a just ruler.</p></div>
